SOAPBOX: Operator age 23
SOAPBOX: Operator is 23 years old (birthday 11/03/2002)
SOAPBOX: This is my first contest in several years and the first contest with my new call (previously, I was KM4SII). I do not have a permanent station at this time, so this was a semi-portable operation from on campus at Auburn University here in Alabama. The antenna was a 10m dipole up about 20 feet on a telescoping painters pole I bought from Home Depot. The antenna was set up outside of my office window between two buildings, so I am sure that hurt performance, but I still could work most of what I could hear.
SOAPBOX: I had high hopes for 10m, but unfortunately the SFI and sunspot number has been falling all week leading up to the contest making conditions rather lackluster. My first QSO was with HK1T at 1230z and the first EU (EI7M) made it in the log at 1309z. Although most of EU was workable to some degree, most stations were not particularly strong. While I could work most everyone I could hear, no EU RBN nodes were hearing me indicating a fairly weak opening. The band closed to EU around 17z and I spent the rest of the afternoon periodically checking the band and picking off the usual South America, West Coast, and KL7/KH6 stations. It was nice to work some semi-uncommon DX -- 8R1TM and ZD7BG. The only Oceanic station I heard aside from the KH6s was ZL60PAH who I was able to work in short order. A JA opening did not really materialize. I could faintly copy JM7OLW, but that was it.
SOAPBOX: Given the unfavorable conditions and the fact that I slept rather poorly before the contest, I do not feel motivated to come back to campus in the morning and set up the temporary antenna again. Still, it was good to get back on the air after an extended QRT! Hopefully I can eventually get a more permeant station set up down here. Thanks for the Qs!
SOAPBOX: 73
SOAPBOX: Mason - N3VLF (ex KM4SII)
